{"type":"message","id":"8715c349","parentId":"a3869c99","timestamp":"2026-03-24T18:44:36.987Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need to respond. The user says: \"Ya estás configurado discord a openclaw... Lo que necesites que analices todo el ecosistema Jarvis... Para ordenar la forma de trabajar en discord... Ahora me entiendes?\" They seem to confirm that Discord is already configured with OpenCLaw, and they want to analyze the entire Jarvis ecosystem to organize how to work in Discord. They ask \"Now do you understand?\" We need to respond accordingly, perhaps by asking clarifying questions about the desired setup. Do we need to use a tool? Possibly we need to read configuration files; maybe there's a config file for discord; maybe it's in TOOLS.md or something. Let's see what files are available.\n\nWe have workspace directory: /home/will/jarvis-ecosystem/agents/jarvis. In that folder we have various files listed: AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, TOOLS.md, IDENTITY.md, USER.md, HEARTBEAT.md, BOOTSTRAP.md. Also there may be other config files for discord. Not listed explicitly. There's a skill \"discord\". The skill directory presumably contains instructions at ~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/discord/SKILL.md. We can read that skill file to understand how discord is configured.\n\nThus we can use the read tool to read that skill file: read path \"~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/discord/SKILL.md\". It will give us content. Then we can understand what configuration is needed. Then we can propose an organized plan.\n\nUser wants to \"analyze everything\" and \"organize the way to work in discord\". Probably they want a plan or suggestions for using discord within the Jarvis ecosystem. Perhaps they want a summary of steps, best practices, channel organization, roles, bots, etc. Also they might want to integrate discord with other parts of the system.\n\nWe can respond by acknowledging understanding and offering to outline a structured approach: reviewing current discord configuration, mapping out tasks, and suggesting organization of channels, bots, automations. Maybe we need to read the skill file for discord to see current config.\n\nThus next step: use read tool to retrieve discord skill file. That is a tool call. Let's do that.\n\nWe will read the discord skill file. Path: \"~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/discord/SKILL.md\". Note that the tool read supports both path and file_path. Use \"path\". Probably correct.\n\nThus call read with path \"~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/discord/SKILL.md\". Then we can parse its content.\n\nAfter reading, we can respond with a summary and ask any clarifications. But we must only do one action per turn; we can either call a tool or send a message. Since we need to read the file first, we will call read. Then in next turn we can provide the answer.\n\nThus call read.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1a4bc3ee953349829ade285a","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/.config/nvm/versions/node/v22.22.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/discord/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openrouter/free","usage":{"input":11846,"output":1448,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13294,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774377848944,"responseId":"gen-1774377852-9zOoAIclPJJiyGxH7CuH"}}
{"type":"message","id":"5a559d5d","parentId":"8715c349","timestamp":"2026-03-24T18:44:37.010Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1a4bc3ee953349829ade285a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: discord\ndescription: \"Discord ops via the message tool (channel=discord).\"\nmetadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎮\", \"requires\": { \"config\": [\"channels.discord.token\"] } } }\nallowed-tools: [\"message\"]\n---\n\n# Discord (Via `message`)\n\nUse the `message` tool. No provider-specific `discord` tool exposed to the agent.\n\n## Musts\n\n- Always: `channel: \"discord\"`.\n- Respect gating: `channels.discord.actions.*` (some default off: `roles`, `moderation`, `presence`, `channels`).\n- Prefer explicit ids: `guildId`, `channelId`, `messageId`, `userId`.\n- Multi-account: optional `accountId`.\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- Avoid Markdown tables in outbound Discord messages.\n- Mention users as `<@USER_ID>`.\n- Prefer Discord components v2 (`components`) for rich UI; use legacy `embeds` only when you must.\n\n## Targets\n\n- Send-like actions: `to: \"channel:<id>\"` or `to: \"user:<id>\"`.\n- Message-specific actions: `channelId: \"<id>\"` (or `to`) + `messageId: \"<id>\"`.\n\n## Common Actions (Examples)\n\nSend message:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"send\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"to\": \"channel:123\",\n  \"message\": \"hello\",\n  \"silent\": true\n}\n```\n\nSend with media:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"send\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"to\": \"channel:123\",\n  \"message\": \"see attachment\",\n  \"media\": \"file:///tmp/example.png\"\n}\n```\n\n- Optional `silent: true` to suppress Discord notifications.\n\nSend with components v2 (recommended for rich UI):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"send\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"to\": \"channel:123\",\n  \"message\": \"Status update\",\n  \"components\": \"[Carbon v2 components]\"\n}\n```\n\n- `components` expects Carbon component instances (Container, TextDisplay, etc.) from JS/TS integrations.\n- Do not combine `components` with `embeds` (Discord rejects v2 + embeds).\n\nLegacy embeds (not recommended):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"send\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"to\": \"channel:123\",\n  \"message\": \"Status update\",\n  \"embeds\": [{ \"title\": \"Legacy\", \"description\": \"Embeds are legacy.\" }]\n}\n```\n\n- `embeds` are ignored when components v2 are present.\n\nReact:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"react\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"channelId\": \"123\",\n  \"messageId\": \"456\",\n  \"emoji\": \"✅\"\n}\n```\n\nRead:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"read\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"to\": \"channel:123\",\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n```\n\nEdit / delete:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"edit\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"channelId\": \"123\",\n  \"messageId\": \"456\",\n  \"message\": \"fixed typo\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"delete\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"channelId\": \"123\",\n  \"messageId\": \"456\"\n}\n```\n\nPoll:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"poll\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"to\": \"channel:123\",\n  \"pollQuestion\": \"Lunch?\",\n  \"pollOption\": [\"Pizza\", \"Sushi\", \"Salad\"],\n  \"pollMulti\": false,\n  \"pollDurationHours\": 24\n}\n```\n\nPins:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"pin\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"channelId\": \"123\",\n  \"messageId\": \"456\"\n}\n```\n\nThreads:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"thread-create\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"channelId\": \"123\",\n  \"messageId\": \"456\",\n  \"threadName\": \"bug triage\"\n}\n```\n\nSearch:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"search\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"guildId\": \"999\",\n  \"query\": \"release notes\",\n  \"channelIds\": [\"123\", \"456\"],\n  \"limit\": 10\n}\n```\n\nPresence (often gated):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"set-presence\",\n  \"channel\": \"discord\",\n  \"activityType\": \"playing\",\n  \"activityName\": \"with fire\",\n  \"status\": \"online\"\n}\n```\n\n## Writing Style (Discord)\n\n- Short, conversational, low ceremony.\n- No markdown tables.\n- Mention users as `<@USER_ID>`.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774377877006}}
