{"type":"message","id":"d994c5fb","parentId":"38a78dad","timestamp":"2026-03-24T18:44:42.429Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6b473ca4a6724b8594b99fc1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"agent\": {\n    \"model\": \"google/gemini-2.5-flash\"\n  },\n  \"agents\": {\n    \"defaults\": {\n      \"model\": \"google/gemini-1.5-flash\",\n      \"fallbacks\": [\n        \"google/gemini-2.0-flash\",\n        \"google/gemini-2.0-flash-lite-preview-02-05\",\n        \"ollama/qwen2.5-coder:0.5b\",\n        \"ollama/phi\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"list\": [\n      { \"id\": \"jarvis\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/jarvis\", \"default\": true },\n      { \"id\": \"mkt-content\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/marketing\" },\n      { \"id\": \"mkt-social\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/marketing\" },\n      { \"id\": \"mkt-analytics\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/marketing\" },\n      { \"id\": \"mkt-ads\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/marketing\" },\n      { \"id\": \"mkt-email\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/marketing\" },\n      { \"id\": \"sales-hunter\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/ventas\" },\n      { \"id\": \"sales-closer\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/ventas\" },\n      { \"id\": \"sales-account\", \"workspace\": \"./agents/ventas\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"bindings\": [\n    { \"agentId\": \"jarvis\", \"match\": { \"channel\": \"whatsapp\", \"accountId\": \"*\" } }\n  ],\n  \"channels\": {\n    \"whatsapp\": {\n      \"dmPolicy\": \"pairing\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"commands\": {\n    \"native\": \"auto\",\n    \"nativeSkills\": \"auto\",\n    \"restart\": true\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774377882425}}
{"type":"message","id":"2855636f","parentId":"d994c5fb","timestamp":"2026-03-24T18:45:02.713Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user indicates that Discord is already configured to OpenClaw and they want to analyze the Jarvis ecosystem to organize how to work in Discord. They ask: \"Ahora me entiendes?\" i.e., \"Do you understand now?\" They want confirmation that we understand and likely want us to proceed with planning.\n\nAs the assistant, we need to respond acknowledging that we understand and perhaps ask for any specific configuration details they want to analyze or setup. Possibly they want us to set up a Discord channel for the Jarvis agent, configure a webhook, assign roles, or maybe create a system for the agent to interact with Discord. They may want to integrate the agent's messages with Discord.\n\nWe have already read the discord skill doc. It shows that to use discord, we need to have a token configured: `channels.discord.token`. The config currently only has `channels.whatsapp` entry. So we might need to add Discord config.\n\nMaybe the user wants to configure the agent to run on Discord as well. The config has \"bindings\" that map agents to channels. It currently binds `jarvis` only to whatsapp. To add Discord, we need to add a binding for Discord channel.\n\nThus we can propose: add Discord entry under `channels` with token, and add binding for the jarvis agent to Discord channel.\n\nBut also they mentioned \"analizar todo el ecosistema Jarvis\" - analyze the whole ecosystem to organize the way to work in Discord. That could involve reviewing all agents, messages, capabilities. Perhaps they want to coordinate which agents should be on Discord.\n\nWe need to interpret the request: Possibly they want to have Jarvis (the main assistant) on Discord, and maybe the specialized agents (marketing, sales, etc.) also on Discord, but perhaps as separate bots or subagents. So we need to design an organization.\n\nWe could respond by summarizing what we see: we have a mult-agent configuration. There is a default agent \"jarvis\" bound to WhatsApp. There are other agents for marketing and sales. Discord config is missing. To work in Discord, we need to add a Discord channel configuration with token and bind the appropriate agents. We can also check if they have a bot token already, if not, guide them through creating one on Discord developer portal.\n\nAlso we may need to define channel names, possibly separate channels for different purposes.\n\nThus we can outline a plan: 1. Gather Discord bot token and application ID. 2. Add channel config: `channels.discord` with token and maybe intents. 3. Bind agents: create binding entries for each agent that should run on Discord. 4. Set up required permissions for bot: read/write messages, manage roles (if needed), etc. 5. Possibly configure webhook for alerts or message routing. 6. Set up presence or status.\n\nWe could also propose to use Discord components for rich interactions.\n\nNow, we should respond to the user's message, confirming understanding and asking clarifying questions to proceed. For instance: \"Yes, entiendo que quieres integrar Discord con el ecosistema Jarvis. Para organizar cómo trabajaremos en Discord, necesito saber: ¿Quieres que sea el agente Jarvis el que se conecte a Discord, o deseas bots separados para cada especialista (marketing, ventas)? ¿Ya tienes un bot de Discord creado con su token? ¿Qué canales o roles específicos te gustaría configurar? ¿Hay alguna funcionalidad en particular (como polls, hilos, reacciones) que quieras habilitar?\"\n\nWe must respect the style guidelines: no filler, be concise but thorough, and ask only needed questions.\n\nWe can also note that current config only binds jarvis to WhatsApp; we need to modify config to include Discord.\n\nThus response: acknowledge and ask clarifications.\n\nWe should also indicate that we can help set up the config and maybe write the necessary changes.\n\nHence response content.\n\nNow we need to respond with appropriate tags. Since this is a direct chat (WhatsApp) from the inbound meta, we use `[[reply_to_current]]` tag.\n\nAlso from the instructions: \"Do not include 'NO_REPLY' in real replies. Use the reply tag.\" So we use reply_to_current.\n\nThus final answer.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]]\nEntiendo. Quieres analizar el ecosistema Jarvis y organizar la forma de trabajar con Discord. Veo que actualmente el agente principal `jarvis` está vinculado solo a WhatsApp y no hay configuración de Discord en `openclaw.json`.\n\nPara avanzar, necesito definir:\n1. **¿Qué agentes deben estar en Discord?** ¿Solo `jarvis` o también los agentes de marketing/ventas? Cada uno podría ser una “cuenta” separada en Discord.\n2. **¿Ya tienes un bot de Discord creado?** Requerimos token y Application ID.\n3. **¿Qué canales y roles usarás?** Podemos mapear canales específicos para diferentes propósitos (soporte, ventas, anuncios).\n4. **¿Qué acciones necesitas?** Enviar mensajes, crear hilos, polls, reacciones, etc.\n\nCon eso puedo ajustar el archivo de configuración y establecer los enlaces. ¿Cuál es tu preferencia?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openrouter/free","usage":{"input":12688,"output":2189,"cacheRead":1024,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15901,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774377882430,"responseId":"gen-1774377883-54vX2grbDLB1fH1QDs2I"}}
